SUMMARY:Jones Falls Ideation Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Brainstorm ideas for improving safety for all road users on Falls Road! \n\n\n\nREGISTER\n\n\n\nIn collaboration with local neighborhood partners—such as the Neighborhood Design Center\, Bikemore\, Blue Water Baltimore\, Rails to Trails\, and Friends of the Jones Falls—and with support from the Maryland Department of Transportation (MDOT) Highway Safety Office\, the MICA Center for Creative Impact is facilitating the Falls Road Safety Project. The goal is to to increase safe behaviors of drivers\, pedestrians\, and bicyclists along Falls Road by: \n\n\n\n\nIdentifying and documenting critical short- and long-term traffic safety issues.\n\n\n\nDeveloping\, testing\, and evaluating creative interventions that increase the safety of all users.\n\n\n\nDeveloping strategies to integrate and implement creative interventions within broader efforts already underway along Falls Road.\n\n\n\n\nThis summer\, MICA is hosting four workshops to brainstorm ideas for improving safety on Falls Road. During each workshop\, participants will: \n\n\n\n\nShare the findings from our research to hear your thoughts\, feedback\, and experiences as user of Falls Road.\n\n\n\nBrainstorm ideas for how to improve safety on Falls Road\, using our findings to guide us.\n\n\n\n\nThere will be four workshops offered in total\, but the content of each workshop will be the same\, so please come to whichever best fits your schedule! \n\n\n\nParticipation is free\, but space is limited! Please register if you plan on attending.
URL:https://bluewaterbaltimore.org/event/jones-falls-ideation-workshop/
LOCATION:MICA Fred Lazarus IV Center Baltimore\, MD 21201\, 131 West North Avenue\, Baltimore\, Maryland\, 21201\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bluewaterbaltimore.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/DJI_20260414113003_0103_D.jpg
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR